Program:
#include <stdio.h>
int sumN(int n)
{
    if (n == 0)
        return 0;
    return n + sumN(n - 1);
}
int main()
{
    int n;
    scanf("%d", &n);
    printf("%d\n", sumN(n));
    return 0;
}
Sample Input:
10
Output:
55
Explanation:
The recursion reduces n by 1 each time. The base case is sumN(0) = 0.
